; DLL search-order hardening (2026-09-24): winhttp.dll is not a KnownDLL, so
; it must not be a static import (see Makefile's DELAY_LIBS comment and
; src/main.c's SetDefaultDllDirectories/SetDllDirectoryW call). This lists
; only the symbols nutshell.exe actually calls -- the AI panel's HTTP client
; (src/ui/ai_http_win.c) and its URL parsing (src/core/ai_tool_web_fetch.c,
; src/core/ai_tool_web_search.c) -- so `dlltool --output-delaylib` can build
; a delay-import library for exactly what's used, no more. Hand-written,
; not gendef'd: gendef needs the real DLL and reads its whole export table,
; which is far more than this build calls.
LIBRARY winhttp.dll
EXPORTS
WinHttpAddRequestHeaders
WinHttpCloseHandle
WinHttpConnect
WinHttpCrackUrl
WinHttpOpen
WinHttpOpenRequest
WinHttpQueryDataAvailable
WinHttpQueryHeaders
WinHttpReadData
WinHttpReceiveResponse
WinHttpSendRequest
WinHttpSetOption
WinHttpSetTimeouts
